# Patch1 has git's a/ and b/ prefixes and edits dir/s.c and z.c. Patch2's ---
# and +++ lines have no prefixes; it makes the same z.c edit and renames dir/s.c
# to dir/t.c with no hunks, so the run picks -p1 and z.c pairs and is left out.
# Patch1's a/dir/s.c strips to dir/s.c, but the rename lines name the source
# without a prefix, so the source must be read as a/dir/s.c before stripping.
# Stripping the bare dir/s.c would give s.c and miss the match. Both sections
# must carry the same notes as in rename-source-depth1.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: patch1 patch2
exit: 0
